    {
      "schema_version": "howl.candidate/v1",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1",
      "source_run_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f",
      "parent_request_id": "cubs-r001-prompt-v2-review-r2",
      "objective": "Independently re-review (round 2, after the author addressed round-1 findings) this proposed change to a campaign execution prompt (the candidate is a unified diff adding section 19A). The prompt's own rules for such changes are in evidence id prompt-s18. Check: contradictions with the rest of the prompt; whether any line weakens or bypasses public-interface use, independent review, evidence, acceptance or merge gates, the pause-and-help rule, the no-local-LLM rule, isolation, or protections for human work; whether it grants new permissions or spending; recovery gaps; unnecessary burden; vague or untestable wording; and whether each lesson's cited trigger justifies it. Use ASSUMPTION lines for problems, CITE for evidence ids, and IDEA only for a concrete wording fix. Evidence id r001-journal holds the journal entries the triggers cite.",
      "text": "ASSUMPTION: Lesson 1 (\"verbatim authorization\") cites journal 2026-10-09T09:35Z, but that entry shows the user's authorization decision at 07:10Z, which is not itself in the supplied journal; whether a recorded dated user instruction exists to quote is unverified.\nCITE: r001-journal\nASSUMPTION: Lesson 1 says \"never infer, paraphrase or broaden\", yet also requires passing it \"in the goal and as a --constraint\". If the authorization is long, verbatim quoting conflicts with a short constraint; the wording does not say whether a quoted excerpt is allowed or only the full text.\nASSUMPTION: Lesson 1 may be read as letting a user authorization override a repository's documented restriction (MLBAM non-bulk). The 04:45Z entry shows those terms are third-party and not the owner's to waive. Lesson 1 and lesson 2 can conflict: authorization to fetch does not authorize bulk publication or bulk fetch. The text says only \"never overrides higher-priority instructions\".\nIDEA: Add to lesson 1: \"An owner authorization does not waive third-party terms; lesson 2 still applies, and authorization to fetch is not authorization to publish.\"\nASSUMPTION: Lesson 1's trigger does not address the S2 root cause fully: the worker was honest and the HowlPlane recorded INCOMPLETE as SUCCEEDED (CUBS-P-008). No lesson covers treating an implementer's declared INCOMPLETE status as a false-success risk, a recovery gap the same trigger supports. Section 18 requires either a prevention instruction or an explicit explanation, and none is recorded for CUBS-P-008.\nCITE: prompt-s18\nASSUMPTION: Lesson 2 thresholds (5 example records, more than 25 records) are arbitrary and unjustified by the trigger. The 04:45Z entry cites roughly 8,600 and 61 records, and the 5-record example allowance may itself breach \"non-bulk\" terms. \"Records copied from source responses\" is also hard to test for transformed or aggregated files; the counting method (for example \"count of API record keys\") is undefined for non-JSON files like patches.\nIDEA: Replace the numbers with \"the count method and threshold are recorded per source after reading its terms, and default to no raw records when terms are ambiguous\".\nASSUMPTION: Lesson 2 does not cover local-only handling of already-fetched bulk data in committed deliverables (cubs-edge-lab research/evidence.json 17 MB), only \"pushes\". It also does not state the scan covers PR/merge commits and not just branch pushes, though section 16 merge may count as public.\nASSUMPTION: Lesson 2 \"ask before any history rewrite\" is consistent with the journal's authority-decision note and adds no permission. Acceptable.\nASSUMPTION: Lesson 3 formula is faithful to the engine.py sizing in the 14:58Z entry: 3 baseline plus 4 of 6 requested gives clamp(6//2,1,3)=3, so 6+3=9 calls were required. It is sound but ties the prompt to an internal engine formula that may change; it needs \"per the tool's current documented sizing\" and a fallback. Also `validate` not warning is a tool defect (NOTE-005), so the prompt change is a workaround and should say so.\nCALC: 6 // 2 = 3\nCALC: 3 + 6 = 9\nCALC: 3 + 4 = 7\nASSUMPTION: Lesson 3 \"pause and ask rather than raise it\" is consistent with section 18's no-spending-authority rule. Fine.\nASSUMPTION: Lesson 4 introduces a possibly new capability: running the public `howl` CLI with PYTHONPATH pointed at a repair worktree before merge. This is arguably a bypass of the \"public-interface use\" gate because it exercises unmerged code and may differ from the installed public interface; the lesson claims it \"supplements\" but the permission is new and its isolation (does it write runtime state or caches?) is unspecified. Also \"Before merge, a committed candidate\" is vague on who runs it.\nIDEA: Add \"read-only for shared runtime state; use a separate state directory or HOME; result is advisory, never evidence for acceptance\".\nASSUMPTION: Lesson 4 \"--verify-timeout at least twice last observed runtime\" assumes a configurable flag. The 17:45Z entry says the 300 s timeout is fixed and undocumented (CUBS-P-004), and no supported configuration can satisfy acceptance. The lesson cannot be followed as written and may be untestable, and its stated trigger (labeled DOG-036) does not match the journal's DOG-035/CUBS-P-004 identifiers. Also the doubled timeout (~912 s) exceeds the 600 s implementer limit noted in the journal.\nCITE: r001-journal\nASSUMPTION: Lesson 4 passing the full gate as --verify may conflict with the journal note that read-only roles cannot run git-invoking tests; it creates a possible deadlock without a pause path.\nASSUMPTION: Lesson 5 cites DOG-039 and \"NOTE-008 at 15:35Z\", which do not appear in the supplied journal. Those triggers are unverified. The observed triggers (CUBS-P-002, CUBS-P-007 readiness downgrades) are present, but CUBS-P-007's cause was Codex quota, and \"documented live doctor\" is an unverified named operation.\nASSUMPTION: Lesson 5 adds a per-session burden (doctor check after every session) with no cost bound; acceptable if cheap but unverified. Its \"trace any downgrade to its cause\" is vague on what counts as traced.\nASSUMPTION: Lesson 6, \"One deliverable stage per session\" is justified by S2 (acquisition plus evaluation coupling) only weakly: S2's failure was missing authorization, not stage mixing. Also \"discard only a mission-owned session\" is a destructive action with no definition of \"mission-owned\", and it may touch human work; the protection for human work should be explicit (never discard sessions or worktrees not created by this campaign). `--separate` is an unverified flag.\nASSUMPTION: Lesson 7 (\"same acceptor judges again, never route to a different acceptor\") conflicts with the journal: in the DOG-035 review, acceptance was rejected by Codex, then Cursor after takeover, and S3's trigger is cited as \"S3 and S3b\", but S3b is absent from the journal. It also weakens independence: a pinned acceptor that rejected for out-of-scope reasons (repository-wide flake8, not a goal criterion) can block indefinitely, and it removes an escape from acceptor error. \"Pause if unavailable\" is a gap-filler, but it forces pause for a recoverable situation.\nIDEA: Replace lesson 7 with \"A different acceptor may be used only with the rejection reasons and acceptance criteria quoted, and recorded; an acceptor's out-of-scope criteria are recorded as findings, not silently adopted\".\nASSUMPTION: Header claim \"They add no authority, remove no gate\" is a self-assertion; Lessons 4 (pre-merge CLI proof) and 7 (acceptor restriction) arguably change authority or gate behavior, so the claim is not verified by the diff alone.\nASSUMPTION: Diff header says v2 \"takes effect at the R002 run boundary\", which matches section 18 activation. Placement at line 836 and the references \"section 16\" and \"section 17\" are unverified because only section 18 was supplied; structural validation (step 5) has no supplied evidence.\nUNKNOWN: independent_review_of_diff_recorded\nUNKNOWN: section_numbering_19A_placement\nCONFLICT: lesson7_acceptor_pinning_vs_journal_takeover_by_different_acceptor",
