  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0/claim/1",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "CITE",
      "text": "prompt-s18",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0/claim/2",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "CITE",
      "text": "r001-journal",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0/claim/3",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 1 (owner authorizations) is justified by the 09:35Z trigger, but the journal shows the actual root cause was the operator's own goal omitting the authorization. The lesson fits. However, \"recorded in the journal\" is untestable if the journal entry was written after the user decision; the wording does not say who records it or when, so a controller could record a paraphrase and then quote it.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0/claim/4",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 1 says to quote the authorization \"as a --constraint\". The constraint may be read by workers as a permission grant. It should state that it only conveys an authorization the user already gave and cannot cover third-party terms (MLBAM non-bulk) unless the user's instruction expressly addressed them. Otherwise it can collide with lesson 2 and with the data-terms incident in the 04:45Z entry.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0/claim/5",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Append to lesson 1: \"An authorization to fetch data does not waive the source's terms; lesson 2 still applies and the quoted text must name the terms it addresses.\"",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0/claim/6",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 2 has a real trigger (04:45Z), but it is internally inconsistent with it. The journal's problem was bulk responses under a \"non-bulk\" term, and \"at most 5 short attributed example records per table\" is a number invented without a reading of the actual terms. It could also exceed what the terms allow, so it reads as a permission. The 25-record threshold likewise lacks a basis. Treat both as defaults that the terms review can only tighten.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0/claim/7",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Reword lesson 2 to: \"Publish nothing beyond what the recorded terms conclusion allows; the 5-record and 25-record figures are upper limits, never grants.\"",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0/claim/8",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 2 \"records copied from source responses\" is vague, since the journal's example counted API record keys. Counting transaction records differs from counting keys, and a scan could be defeated by encoded, compressed or patch-format files (the leaked items were .patch files and probe_results.json). The wording should name the formats covered, including patches and archives.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0/claim/9",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 2 recovery gap: the 04:45Z incident left bulk data in public branch history. The lesson covers \"already reached a public branch\" by pausing, which is good. It does not cover the local private/ copies or what happens to unpushed commits that contain bulk data, so the push-blocking rule could be satisfied while history still carries the data.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0/claim/10",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 3 (Dream sizing) has a valid trigger (14:58Z), and the formula matches the journal's engine.py description. It is only operator-observed, though, and the formula could change with engine versions. \"Record the number\" is testable. The \"pause and ask rather than raise\" language is consistent with no new spending. Low risk.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0/claim/11",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 4 is the riskiest. Its trigger (17:45Z, DOG-036) does not appear under that ID in the journal, which cites DOG-035 and CUBS-P-004. The citation is unsupported, which is a trigger mismatch.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0/claim/12",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 4's \"at least twice its last observed runtime\" for --verify-timeout is a new budget-like setting. CUBS-P-004 says the orchestration timeout is fixed at 300 s and not configurable, so the instruction may be impossible to follow, and the journal says no supported session configuration can satisfy it. The lesson presents a fix for a defect the journal calls unfixable at the prompt level. It should say to pause if the flag is unsupported.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0/claim/13",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 4 allows proving a committed candidate with the public `howl` CLI with PYTHONPATH pointing at an unmerged worktree. This is a new execution path outside prior text. It could weaken the public-interface rule, since running unmerged code via PYTHONPATH is not the installed public interface, and it risks being read as pre-merge acceptance. The \"supplements and never replaces\" clause helps but needs an explicit \"does not count as public proof\".",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0/claim/14",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 5 (agents doctor) has valid triggers (CUBS-P-002, CUBS-P-007). The journal labels the second incident CUBS-P-007, not DOG-039, so the citation mismatches. \"Documented live doctor\" is undefined and unverifiable in the supplied evidence. Burden is added by checking after every session.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0/claim/15",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 6 has two rules bundled: stage separation and worktree handling. The S2 trigger supports separating acquisition from evaluation only loosely (the cause was the missing authorization, not the stage mix). NOTE-008 is not in the supplied evidence, so the `--separate` and discard rules are unsupported. \"Discard only a mission-owned session\" touches human-work protections; \"mission-owned\" is undefined and could allow deleting a human's session.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0/claim/16",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "In lesson 6, replace discard with \"never discard; archive and ask unless ownership is recorded in the journal\".",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0/claim/17",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 7 (same acceptor) is a weakness. The S3 trigger shows the acceptor rejected for flake8 violations in pre-existing files, outside the goal criteria. Pinning the same acceptor and passing its reasons into the goal can let a possibly wrong rejection steer the work. Forbidding a different acceptor removes an independence check, and the lesson relies on S3b, which is not in the journal. It also conflicts with pause-on-unavailable if the acceptor stays conflicted.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0/claim/18",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Header claim \"add no authority, remove no gate\" is a self-assertion. Lessons 4 and 7 plausibly change authority (a new execution path and a restricted acceptor choice), so section 18 step 4 independent review must test them, not rely on the header.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0/claim/19",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "The diff contains no lesson for the CUBS-P-008 false-success trigger (INCOMPLETE recorded as SUCCEEDED), which section 18 says to cover or explain. The omission is not recorded in the diff. The same applies to CUBS-P-003 and CUBS-P-004.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0/claim/20",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "diff_version_effective_boundary_validation",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0/claim/21",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "section_references_in_diff_19A_vs_existing_sections_16_17",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/1",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Bullet 1 (verbatim authorization) is justified by the 09:35Z trigger, but the journal never records that the authorization was ever absent from the goal in dated form; the journal says only that \"my goal did not state the owner's explicit authorization\", so \"verbatim quote\" is a plausible fix, not a proven one.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/2",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "CITE",
      "text": "r001-journal",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/3",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Bullet 1 says \"Only an explicit, dated instruction from the user that is recorded in the journal may be passed on\", but it gives no recovery step when the user instruction exists only in conversation and was never journaled (as in the 07:10Z decision). A worker could be blocked again, and \"pause under section 17\" is only stated for unclear scope.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/4",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Add to bullet 1: \"If the instruction is not yet journaled, journal it with date and verbatim text before launching the session.\"",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/5",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Bullet 1 uses `--constraint` as the carrier for an authorization. Worker-visible constraints could be read as granting repository-restricted actions (for example bulk fetching despite MLBAM terms). This sits in tension with bullet 2, which forbids bulk publication, and with prompt-s18's ban on granting new permissions. The text should say an authorization covers only the stated action and not publication.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/6",
