    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/7",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Bullet 2's scan is a \"count of records copied from source responses\" with a threshold of 25 per staged file. The journal trigger shows files of about 8,600 and 61 records, and the 61-record file was also a problem. The 25 threshold and the \"5 example records per table\" cap are invented numbers with no cited basis, so they are arbitrary. Counting \"records copied from source responses\" is also hard to test for patches, JSON blobs, and renamed keys.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/8",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "CITE",
      "text": "r001-journal",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/9",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Replace the threshold with \"any staged file containing source-response records beyond the permitted examples blocks the push\", and name the counting method, such as counting occurrences of the source's record keys, as the journal does.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/10",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Bullet 2 says to pause and ask \"before any history rewrite\", which is consistent with the journal (a rewrite is an authority decision). It does not say what to do about branch history that already contains bulk data, such as taking the branch private or deleting it. This leaves a recovery gap, though that may be intentional.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/11",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Bullet 2 says to \"read the source's terms\", yet the trigger shows the terms were visible in the response payloads (a copyright notice) and were not read before pushing. The lesson is justified, but \"terms\" should include notices embedded in API responses, not only a web page.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/12",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Reword bullet 2 to \"read the source's terms, including any notice embedded in its responses\".",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/13",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Bullet 3 (Dream budget) is justified by the 14:58Z trigger, since the journal gives the formula clamp(max_candidates//2,1,3)+max_candidates. The journal also says the formula comes from engine.py, so it is an engine internal that can drift. The bullet hardcodes it and should point to the tool's `validate` output or say \"verify against the current engine\". The bullet does correctly avoid raising the approved budget and says to pause, which is consistent with s18.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/14",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "CITE",
      "text": "prompt-s18",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/15",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Bullet 4 (Howl repair) has a possible conflict. The trigger is dated 17:45Z, but its findings are CUBS-P-004: the verify timeout is a fixed, undocumented 300 s, and no supported configuration can satisfy it. Telling the operator to set `--verify-timeout` to at least twice the runtime assumes that flag exists and takes effect, and the journal says it doesn't. The instruction could be untestable or impossible. The citation \"DOG-036\" is also absent from the journal text provided, so the trigger is not verified.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/16",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "CITE",
      "text": "r001-journal",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/17",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Rewrite bullet 4 to say \"if the engine cannot honor a verify timeout covering the full gate, record CUBS-P-004 and pause under section 17; do not narrow --verify\".",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/18",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Bullet 4's allowance to prove a committed candidate \"through the public `howl` CLI with PYTHONPATH pointing at a clean repair worktree\" is a new execution path not found in the cited evidence. It may weaken the public-interface rule, since PYTHONPATH redirection means running unmerged code through the CLI, and might be read as bypassing the isolation rules or the shared engine. The text says it \"supplements\" the gates, which helps, but it is new and has no trigger in the journal.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/19",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Bullet 5 (agents doctor check) cites \"DOG-039\" and \"NOTE-008\", ids the journal does not show. CUBS-P-002 and CUBS-P-007 are in the journal. Citations to unseen ids cannot be tested. The bullet's example, \"the documented live doctor\", is vague, since the journal does not say what that command is. \"Trace any downgrade to its cause\" has no stated stopping condition, which adds burden after every session.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/20",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "CITE",
      "text": "r001-journal",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/21",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Bullet 6 conflates two rules. \"One deliverable stage per session\" is supported by the S2 block, but the S2 root cause was a missing authorization, not a stage mix. The journal shows S2 mixing was not the failure, so the trigger does not justify it. The \"discard only a mission-owned session\" clause permits deleting work, which touches protections for human work. The phrase \"mission-owned\" is undefined, and preserving a patch only protects uncommitted work, not other artifacts.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/22",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Define \"mission-owned\" as \"created by this campaign and recorded in the handoff\", and drop the stage rule or cite a real trigger.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/23",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Bullet 7 (same acceptor) is the weakest. The S3 trigger shows the acceptor rejected for flake8 in pre-existing files, outside the goal criteria. Pinning the same acceptor reinforces the biased judge, and \"never route to a different acceptor\" removes a possible independence mechanism and could cause a deadlock. It may weaken independent review and acceptance, because the journal shows no S3b, and the acceptor's own demand was the problem. Pausing if \"unavailable or conflicted\" is undefined for \"conflicted\".",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/24",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Replace bullet 7 with \"when an acceptance rejection cites criteria not in the goal, record it as a finding and pause under section 17 for a decision; do not switch acceptors on your own.\"",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/25",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "The lead sentence states \"add no authority, remove no gate, and do not change budgets\", but the claim is only a statement and does not ensure it. Bullets 4 and 6 plausibly add execution paths and discard rights, so the claim is untested. The effective-date rule (\"takes effect at the R002 run boundary\") is consistent with s18.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/26",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "s18 step 3 requires recording the triggering evidence per change. The diff ties triggers by date, but several bullets (4, 5, 6, 7) cite ids absent from the supplied journal, so I cannot confirm the justification.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/27",
