      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "trigger-evidence-for-DOG-036-DOG-039-NOTE-008-S3b",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0/claim/28",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "independent-review-of-this-diff-via-Howl-path",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1/claim/1",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 1 (\"verbatim authorization\") cites journal 2026-10-09T09:35Z, but that entry shows the user's authorization decision at 07:10Z, which is not itself in the supplied journal; whether a recorded dated user instruction exists to quote is unverified.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1/claim/2",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "CITE",
      "text": "r001-journal",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1/claim/3",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 1 says \"never infer, paraphrase or broaden\", yet also requires passing it \"in the goal and as a --constraint\". If the authorization is long, verbatim quoting conflicts with a short constraint; the wording does not say whether a quoted excerpt is allowed or only the full text.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1/claim/4",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 1 may be read as letting a user authorization override a repository's documented restriction (MLBAM non-bulk). The 04:45Z entry shows those terms are third-party and not the owner's to waive. Lesson 1 and lesson 2 can conflict: authorization to fetch does not authorize bulk publication or bulk fetch. The text says only \"never overrides higher-priority instructions\".",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1/claim/5",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Add to lesson 1: \"An owner authorization does not waive third-party terms; lesson 2 still applies, and authorization to fetch is not authorization to publish.\"",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1/claim/6",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 1's trigger does not address the S2 root cause fully: the worker was honest and the HowlPlane recorded INCOMPLETE as SUCCEEDED (CUBS-P-008). No lesson covers treating an implementer's declared INCOMPLETE status as a false-success risk, a recovery gap the same trigger supports. Section 18 requires either a prevention instruction or an explicit explanation, and none is recorded for CUBS-P-008.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1/claim/7",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "CITE",
      "text": "prompt-s18",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1/claim/8",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 2 thresholds (5 example records, more than 25 records) are arbitrary and unjustified by the trigger. The 04:45Z entry cites roughly 8,600 and 61 records, and the 5-record example allowance may itself breach \"non-bulk\" terms. \"Records copied from source responses\" is also hard to test for transformed or aggregated files; the counting method (for example \"count of API record keys\") is undefined for non-JSON files like patches.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1/claim/9",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Replace the numbers with \"the count method and threshold are recorded per source after reading its terms, and default to no raw records when terms are ambiguous\".",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1/claim/10",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 2 does not cover local-only handling of already-fetched bulk data in committed deliverables (cubs-edge-lab research/evidence.json 17 MB), only \"pushes\". It also does not state the scan covers PR/merge commits and not just branch pushes, though section 16 merge may count as public.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1/claim/11",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 2 \"ask before any history rewrite\" is consistent with the journal's authority-decision note and adds no permission. Acceptable.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1/claim/12",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 3 formula is faithful to the engine.py sizing in the 14:58Z entry: 3 baseline plus 4 of 6 requested gives clamp(6//2,1,3)=3, so 6+3=9 calls were required. It is sound but ties the prompt to an internal engine formula that may change; it needs \"per the tool's current documented sizing\" and a fallback. Also `validate` not warning is a tool defect (NOTE-005), so the prompt change is a workaround and should say so.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1/claim/13",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "CALC",
      "text": "6 // 2 = 3",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
