      "kind": "CALC",
      "text": "3 + 6 = 9",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1/claim/15",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "CALC",
      "text": "3 + 4 = 7",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1/claim/16",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 3 \"pause and ask rather than raise it\" is consistent with section 18's no-spending-authority rule. Fine.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1/claim/17",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 4 introduces a possibly new capability: running the public `howl` CLI with PYTHONPATH pointed at a repair worktree before merge. This is arguably a bypass of the \"public-interface use\" gate because it exercises unmerged code and may differ from the installed public interface; the lesson claims it \"supplements\" but the permission is new and its isolation (does it write runtime state or caches?) is unspecified. Also \"Before merge, a committed candidate\" is vague on who runs it.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1/claim/18",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Add \"read-only for shared runtime state; use a separate state directory or HOME; result is advisory, never evidence for acceptance\".",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1/claim/19",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 4 \"--verify-timeout at least twice last observed runtime\" assumes a configurable flag. The 17:45Z entry says the 300 s timeout is fixed and undocumented (CUBS-P-004), and no supported configuration can satisfy acceptance. The lesson cannot be followed as written and may be untestable, and its stated trigger (labeled DOG-036) does not match the journal's DOG-035/CUBS-P-004 identifiers. Also the doubled timeout (~912 s) exceeds the 600 s implementer limit noted in the journal.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1/claim/20",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "CITE",
      "text": "r001-journal",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1/claim/21",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 4 passing the full gate as --verify may conflict with the journal note that read-only roles cannot run git-invoking tests; it creates a possible deadlock without a pause path.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1/claim/22",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 5 cites DOG-039 and \"NOTE-008 at 15:35Z\", which do not appear in the supplied journal. Those triggers are unverified. The observed triggers (CUBS-P-002, CUBS-P-007 readiness downgrades) are present, but CUBS-P-007's cause was Codex quota, and \"documented live doctor\" is an unverified named operation.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1/claim/23",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190200-07312665f66f/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Lesson 5 adds a per-session burden (doctor check after every session) with no cost bound; acceptable if cheap but unverified. Its \"trace any downgrade to its cause\" is vague on what counts as traced.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
